      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if the confidence interval was wider, like [-0.05, 0.50], even if the p-value was still low, how would that change the interpretation of the \"reliability\" of the finding? i'm trying to understand how much weight i can actually put on the result when there's a lot of variance in the sample.",
