      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A wider confidence interval, such as [-0.05, 0.50], indicates greater uncertainty or variability in your sample data. Even with a statistically significant p-value, this wide interval suggests that while the true effect *could* be positive, it is also plausible that the true effect might be very small or even slightly negative. Therefore, you must acknowledge that the precision of your estimate is lower, meaning the magnitude of the effect size is less reliably pinned down.",
